      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's important not to give your baby any juice since it can lead to more diarrhea and potential dehydration. Seek medical attention immediately. Babies with severe diarrhea and those who are not drinking can quickly become dangerously dehydrated, especially if they're not having wet diapers for an extended period. Bring them to the emergency room or contact your pediatrician as soon as possible.",
